  "kind": "SURFACE",
  "status": "exists",
  "docs": {
    "purpose": "An operator's project watchlist. Saved permits and Committee-of-Adjustment items are grouped into three bands - needs attention, starting soon, and further out - and paged; a search box finds any Toronto address to add, tick-boxes allow removing several at once behind a confirmation, and clicking a row opens a side panel with the full record plus a prominent header saying whether the project looks delayed and when it is expected to start. Nothing is auto-archived: finished projects stay until an operator deletes them.",
    "data_story": "It reads nothing from the database directly. Every value arrives through 3 contracts: `/api/admin/leads/watchlist`, `/api/admin/leads/watchlist/search`, `/api/admin/leads/inspect/[id]`. Behind those contracts, the data comes from `admin_watchlist`, `building_footprints`, `coa_applications`, `cost_estimates`, `entities`, `lead_trades`, `lead_views`, `lifecycle_status_history`, `logic_variables`, `neighbourhoods`, `parcel_buildings`, `parcels`, `permit_parcels`, `permit_phase_transitions`, `permit_trades`, `permits`, `phase_stay_calibration`, `scope_intensity_matrix`, `trade_forecasts`, `trades` and `universal_stream_catalog`, and writes land on `admin_watchlist`.",
    "under_126": "**REBUILD** — it drives writes, so a client decision has to be re-homed on the server before the projection can be honest. It renders through the LIST renderer (a collection with declared pagination, recycling and empty/offline states), reading by reference: `/api/admin/leads/watchlist`, `/api/admin/leads/watchlist/search`, `/api/admin/leads/inspect/[id]`. Its `owns.components[]` declares `src/components/admin/FlightCenterTool.tsx` and `src/components/admin/SearchPermitsModal.tsx`."
  },
